WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Go back before Rumfa, to King Abdullahi Burja. People already lived inside the first wall.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:10.000
The Chronicle says Burja opened roads from Bornu, in the east, to Gwanja, in the south-west.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
He was the first in Hausaland to own camels.

4
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:21.000
He was also the first to send tribute to Bornu. His men raided the south for captives, and settled them in twenty-one new towns.

5
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Under Yakubu, Fulani came from Mali with books on divinity and etymology. Salt became common in Hausaland.

6
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.400
Then came Rumfa: his palace, new walls through named gates, and Kurmi market.

7
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.000
Traders and scholars came to the city.

8
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Rumfa gave offices of state to eunuchs, and began a council of nine, the Tara-ta-Kano.

9
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
He began kulle, the seclusion of women, and was the first to have kakaki, long royal trumpets.

10
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.000
In his time came Kano's first war with Katsina. It lasted eleven years, and neither side won.

11
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Writing in 1526, Leo Africanus described Kano's people as wealthy merchants and skilled craftsmen. Whether he ever went there is doubted. By then, Wangara merchants had probably brought kola nuts into the trade.
